  "content": "<p><strong>Unit 2 - Percent — Title &amp; Goal</strong><br />Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 2 - Percent for SAT Math preparation.</p>\n\n\n<h3>Key idea</h3>\n<p>Read the idea and scan the rules. Focus on how the symbols behave.</p>\n<p>A <strong>percent</strong> is a ratio out of 100.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mtext>Percent</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>Part</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>Whole</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>100</mn></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li>50% = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> </li>\n<li>25% = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> </li>\n<li>200% = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>200</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> </li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<h3>Formula</h3>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mtext>PercentÂ Change</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>New</mtext><mo>âˆ’</mo><mtext>Original</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>Original</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>100</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li>Positive → increase  </li>\n<li>Negative → decrease  </li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Linear growth</strong>: constant <strong>addition</strong> per step<br/>\n  Example: salary increases \\<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2000</mn><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>â†’</mi></mrow></math>y=2000t+P$  </li>\n<li><strong>Exponential growth</strong>: constant <strong>multiplication</strong> per step<br/>\n  Example: bacteria doubles every hour → <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> </li>\n</ul>\n<p>1) Convert: (a) 0.2 to percent, (b) 150% to decimal.<br/>\n2) Find percent change: 60 → 45.<br/>\n3) Simple interest: $800 at 6% for 2 years.<br/>\n4) Compound interest: $500 at 8% annually for 2 years.<br/>\n5) Linear growth: population starts at 1000, grows by 50 per year. Write equation.<br/>\n6) Exponential decay: medicine amount starts at 200 mg, halves each hour. Write equation.<br/>\n7) Identify association:<br/>\n   - Number of hours worked vs. income.<br/>\n   - Hours of TV watched vs. GPA.  </p>\n<p>1) (a) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math> (b) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>150</mn><mi>%</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math> (decrease)<br/>\n3) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.06</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n4) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1.08</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>583.20</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n5) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></math><br/>\n6) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></math><br/>\n7) Positive: hours worked vs. income. Negative: TV hours vs. GPA.</p>\n\n<h3>Worked example</h3>\n<p>Follow the steps carefully, then try to reproduce them without looking.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples</strong><br/>\n1. Price from \\<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>40</mn><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>\\</mi></mrow></math>50:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>%</mi><mtext>Â increase</mtext></mrow></math>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>Price from \\<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>80</mn><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>\\</mi></mrow></math>60:  </li>\n</ol>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>80</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>%</mi><mtext>Â decrease</mtext></mrow></math>\n<h3>Simple Interest</h3>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math> = principal  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math> = rate (decimal)  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> = time  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong>: \\<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>I = 1000(0.05)(3)=150$  </p>\n<h3>Compound Interest</h3>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math> = total  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math> = principal  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math> = annual rate (decimal)  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></math> = times compounded per year  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> = time in years  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong>: $1000 at 5% compounded annually for 3 years  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1.05</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1157.63</mn></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br/>\n40% of students are girls. If there are 200 students, how many are girls?  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.40</mn><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>200</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong><br/>\nAn item is discounted 20%, then taxed 5%. If original price is $100:<br/>\n- After discount: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n- After tax: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1.05</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>84</mn></mrow></math> </p>\n<p><strong>Linear growth/decay equation:</strong></p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>: growth  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>: decay  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br/>\nA tank loses 5 liters per hour, starting with 200:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>General formula:</strong></p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>Â±</mi><mi>r</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></math> for growth  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>âˆ’</mo></mrow></math> for decay  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br/>\nCar worth $20,000 depreciates 10% per year:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20000</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.9</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Positive association</strong>: as <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> increases, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></math> tends to increase.  </li>\n<li><strong>Negative association</strong>: as <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> increases, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></math> tends to decrease.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Examples</strong>\n- Hours studied vs. test score → positive<br/>\n- Speed vs. travel time → negative  </p>\n\n<h3>Quick practice</h3>\n<p>Try these on your own. Check your steps, not just the final answer.</p>\n1) Convert: (a) 0.2 to percent, (b) 150% to decimal.<br/>\n<br />\n1) (a) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math> (b) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>150</mn><mi>%</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n2) Find percent change: 60 → 45.<br/>\n<br />\n2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math> (decrease)<br/>\n\n3) Simple interest: $800 at 6% for 2 years.<br/>\n<br />\n3) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.06</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n<h3>Mixed practice set</h3>\n<p>These mix everything above. Time yourself and reflect on any mistakes.</p>\n\n4) Compound interest: $500 at 8% annually for 2 years.<br/>\n<br />\n4) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1.08</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>583.20</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n5) Linear growth: population starts at 1000, grows by 50 per year. Write equation.<br/>\n<br />\n5) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></math><br/>\n\n6) Exponential decay: medicine amount starts at 200 mg, halves each hour. Write equation.<br/>\n<br />\n6) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></math><br/>\n\n7) Identify association:<br/>\n   - Number of hours worked vs. income.<br/>\n   - Hours of TV watched vs. GPA.  \n<br />\n7) Positive: hours worked vs. income. Negative: TV hours vs. GPA.",
